build*/
cmake-build-*/
test/
# `test/` above is unanchored, so it matches a `test` directory at ANY depth,
# not just the local build scratch dir it is grouped with. That silently
# swallowed .github/scripts/test/, which runner-names-validate.yml runs. Keep
# the broad rule (a nested test/ elsewhere may rely on it) and re-include the
# CI path. The directory itself has to be re-included: git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded.
!.github/scripts/test/
.vscode/
.idea/
.cache/
*.swp
*.bat
*.bin
*.exe
*.gguf
output*.png
models*
*.log
preview.png
